WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.850
Speaker 1: I want to talk a little bit about
book banning.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:08.840
One of the comments that I'm seeing pretty
regularly on the shorts, YouTube shorts that

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:15.530
I post about Republican book banning efforts
is people commenting and saying banning these

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:22.630
books is good because they're only banning
pornographic books and books that aren't age

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:23.680
appropriate.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.220
Let me show you some of the comments that
I've been receiving.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:33.309
I won't even name the these are just YouTube
people with long strings as their usernames,

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:34.650
but here are some of the comments.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.120
How is banning a porno book on a middle school
library Fascism, isn't it?

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.060
At worst, censorship based on age and at best,
parenting and protecting children from losing

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.559
their innocence sooner than necessary.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:46.629
It's not fascism.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:53.340
If it's inappropriate content for kids, schlock
of God says no, Banning books that are not

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.100
appropriate for kids is morally correct.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:01.910
JP Music says there's a huge difference between
limiting what books schools can have available

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:08.590
for kids and removing books from public libraries
or not allowing the sale of certain books,

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.939
JD says.

00:01:09.939 --> 00:01:12.580
Have you looked at the content of the books?

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.520
Many are pornographic in nature.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:21.360
Dr. Och says it depends on what books are
being banned.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.860
Planet Positivity says false when it applies
to children.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:31.000
Extremists on the far left and right want
their propaganda taught to kids and both are

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.770
age inappropriate.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:36.270
Jan says it's critical that parents be able
to make these decisions.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.020
I don't want the government deciding what
my kid can and can't read.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:45.360
But Billy Beans said restrictions imposed
by parents are equally bad as restrictions

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.720
imposed by governments, if not worse.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.290
Jay says banning books is not the same as
removing nine age appropriate books from elementary

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.110
school libraries.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.250
So I decided to look at some of the books
that are being banned, and you can easily

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.220
find these these lists.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:05.399
Penn dot org has a list, and here are some
of the books that are regularly banned.

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:15.970
One is called Genderqueer a memoir, and it's
about a person who uses pronouns like air

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:19.310
and explains why to their family.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:22.129
This one has been banned more than 40 times.

00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:32.610
All Boys Aren't Blue by George Johnson, which
is a series of essays from an LGBT activist

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.220
that explores his childhood and adolescence.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.290
Out of Darkness by Ashley Hope Perez.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:47.000
A dangerous, forbidden romance rocks a Texas
oil town in 1937, when segregation was a matter

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.780
of life and death.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.330
The Bluest Eye by Toni Morrison.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:57.240
Because it obsesses, it examines our obsession
with beauty and conformity.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.070
And you can go through these and you can get
a bigger list.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.670
And this is going to be sort of hard to see
because of the zoom.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.610
But you see that there are all these different
books that have been banned.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.959
Some have been banned by administrators.

00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:12.769
Some have been challenged by parents.

00:03:12.769 --> 00:03:15.020
You see all these different examples.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:20.640
And I have to tell you, I spent time randomly
picking these books and I went to Amazon and

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.220
I did the look inside and I read, you know,
a number of pages that are available.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:31.510
The vast majority of these books are neither
pornographic nor extreme.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:38.140
However, many of them do have storylines that
it seems many right wingers don't like.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.910
Sometimes there are gay characters.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.030
That's it.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.939
So they want the book banned.

00:03:44.939 --> 00:03:52.730
Sometimes there are descriptions of sexual
encounters and we could have a conversation.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.750
Is that appropriate for seven year olds?

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.050
Well, maybe not.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:59.310
But is it appropriate for high school juniors?

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.330
Yeah, it's fine.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:07.880
In some of them, there are descriptions of
non-binary people, or whatever the case may

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.880
be.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:15.330
The overwhelming majority of these books are
not pornographic and.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:22.290
It is very clear that a lot of the people
saying it's good to ban these books have absolutely

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.690
no idea what is in the books.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.700
I also want to say another thing.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.330
A lot of these books don't seem that great
to me.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.919
And what I mean by it is I'm not saying.

00:04:34.919 --> 00:04:39.210
A lot of this stuff is just personal preference
at the end of the day, right?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Like, what kind of stuff do you enjoy reading?

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:47.950
A lot of these books, as I look at them, aren't
particularly titillating, but they also don't

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.150
seem particularly interesting to me.

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:55.450
And it seems to me that making a big deal
for any reason out of these books just doesn't

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.479
really make sense.

00:04:56.479 --> 00:05:01.250
If this is a book that a teacher wants to
have in a curriculum.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:05.009
It just seems very strange to get all shaken
up about it.

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:09.350
And what I was reminded of, of course, is
that the right wingers that want a lot of

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.000
these books banned are really the snowflakes.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.800
They love to say, Oh, the left is so sensitive.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.490
The left can't handle anything and all these
different things.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:20.650
I mean, listen.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.009
Gay relationships exist.

00:05:23.009 --> 00:05:24.760
Slavery existed.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.670
Brutality existed.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.690
Non-binary people exist.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:35.789
And just saying that the inclusion of that
those as topics is, quote, inappropriate for,

00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:40.050
quote, kids, particularly when a lot of them
don't distinguish between a first grader and

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.600
a high school junior senior.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.039
They seem to be exposing themselves as the
snowflakes that can't handle.

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:51.150
And if anything and you know, I don't want
to go too far down this path, but if you look

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:58.131
at historical efforts to ban, you know, so-called
degenerate art, as Nazis wanted to do, if

00:05:58.131 --> 00:06:02.639
you look at all other efforts that we've seen
over time from authoritarian leaning movements

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:08.940
and leaders to control media and books and
publications, it's really ugly stuff.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.050
And quite frankly, it mostly seems to backfire.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.910
So take a look at the books that they actually
want to ban.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:19.470
Go on Amazon, click on Look Inside, look,
read a little bit, and you will very quickly

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.819
